pconsole 1.2.0 - guard every seteuid() call site with a POSIX no-op test

pconsole drops/regains privileges by calling seteuid() unconditionally.
There are exactly three such call sites in pconsole.c, and all three are
on paths the program actually executes:

  line 104  put_conn()  seteuid(0)         "regain root privs", before the
                                         ioctl(TIOCSTI) of every keystroke
  line 115  put_conn()  seteuid(getuid())  "drop root privs again", the
                                         mandatory tail of every keystroke
                                         injection
  line 227  main()      seteuid(getuid())  "drop root privs", at startup

When the effective uid already equals the real uid those calls cannot
change anything - they are no-ops by definition, and the kernel's own
set_user() fast path skips its capability check for them.  On a platform
that refuses the privileged id syscall from a process that holds no such
privilege (e.g. the seccomp whitelist of OpenHarmony/HarmonyOS, which
kills the process with an uncatchable SIGSYS / exit 159 before the
syscall ever returns) the program therefore dies even though there was
nothing to drop.  Because line 115 is the tail of put_conn(), that is the
path every single injected keystroke takes, so leaving it unguarded keeps
the program fatal on precisely its core feature.

Skip the syscall when it is provably a no-op.  The predicate is plain
POSIX (geteuid/getuid), so no platform macro is involved and behaviour
on every other platform is unchanged: a real setuid-root binary still
takes the original path and still reports the original error.

A regression guard lives in test_package/pconsole_pty_test.py (H5): it
installs a seccomp-bpf filter that traps the whole set*-id syscall family
in the child before exec, which reproduces the HarmonyOS boundary, and
then drives a real keystroke injection through put_conn().  A build that
emits any privileged id syscall on that path dies by SIGSYS and the test
fails; the fully guarded build issues none and survives.

--- a/pconsole.c
+++ b/pconsole.c
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* regain root privs */
-	if (seteuid(0)) {
+	if (geteuid() != getuid() && seteuid(0)) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "failed to regain root privs: %s\n", strerror(errno));
 		cmd_exit(NULL);
 		/* unreached */
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
 	saved_errno = errno;
 
 	/* drop root privs again */
-	if (seteuid(getuid())) {
+	if (geteuid() != getuid() && seteuid(getuid())) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "failed to drop root privs: %s\n", strerror(errno));
 		cmd_exit(NULL);
 		/* unreached */
@@ -224,7 +224,7 @@
 		fprintf(stderr, "You must be root to run this program or this program should be setuid root.\n");
 		return -1;
 	}
-	if (seteuid(getuid())) {				/* drop root privs */
+	if (geteuid() != getuid() && seteuid(getuid())) {		/* drop root privs */
 		fprintf(stderr, "failed to drop root privileges\n");
 		exit(-1);
 	}
